{{Short description|Football tournament}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
The knockout stage of [[1974 FIFA World Cup]] was a [[single-elimination tournament]] involving the four teams that qualified from [[1974 FIFA World Cup#Second round|the second group stage of the tournament]]. There were two matches: a match for third place contested by the group runners-up, and the final to decide the champions, contested by the group winners.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/74full.html |title=World Cup 1974 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> The knockout stage began with the match for third place on 6 July and ended with the [[1974 FIFA World Cup final|final]] on 7 July 1974, both at the [[Olympiastadion (Munich)|Olympiastadion]] in [[Munich]]. [[Germany national football team|West Germany]] won the tournament with a 2–1 victory over the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]].<ref>{{cite web |url = http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2006/4850426.stm |title = World Cup history - West Germany 1974 |work = BBC Sport |publisher = British Broadcasting Corporation |date = 4 May 2006 |accessdate = 27 July 2012}}</ref>

==Qualified teams==
The top two placed teams from each of the two groups of the second round qualified for the knockout stage.

